<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zwiefalten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zwiefalten is a municipality in the district of Reutlingen in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-jura">Swabian Jura</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It grew around a Benedictine abbey founded in 1089 by the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achalm">Achalm</a> and settled from Hirsau, which became an imperial abbey in 1750. Its church, rebuilt from 1739 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-michael-fischer">Johann Michael Fischer</a> with stucco by Johann Michael Feichtmayr and frescoes by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-spiegler">Franz Joseph Spiegler</a>, is a masterpiece of the late baroque.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zwiefalten.jpg" alt="Zwiefalten" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zwiefalten_in_RT.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
